      "The governing equation is hyperbolic; hyperbolicity is part of the definition of the problem [printed p. 5, Section 1.2.1, “the hyperbolic equation together with special initial data”].",
      "The initial data are constant on each side of one interface and are described as having a single jump discontinuity [printed p. 5, Section 1.2.1, opening paragraph]."
    ],
    "conclusions": [
      "A Riemann problem consists of the hyperbolic equation together with the specified two-state initial data [printed p. 5, Section 1.2.1, opening definition].",
      "For every x < 0, the prescribed initial value is q(x,0) = q_l; for every x > 0, it is q(x,0) = q_r [printed p. 5, equation (1.11)]."
