      "For the linear constant-coefficient specialization q_t + A q_x = 0, A is a constant real m × m matrix, and hyperbolicity means real eigenvalues with m linearly independent corresponding eigenvectors [printed p. 1, equation (1.1) and following text; printed p. 3, opening paragraph].",
      "The selected passage is a definition of problem data, not an existence or uniqueness theorem for solutions [printed p. 5, Section 1.2.1, opening sentence and equation (1.11)]."
    ],
