      "The chapter concerns time-dependent, first-order hyperbolic equations and systems; the selected Riemann problem is one-dimensional [printed p. 1, introductory discussion; printed p. 3, “we only consider first-order hyperbolic systems”; printed p. 6, Section 1.3, “inherently one-dimensional”].",
      "Nonlinear conservation laws are included in the surrounding setting; imposing constant linear coefficients on every Riemann problem would restrict the definition beyond its stated scope [printed pp. 3–4, Section 1.1; printed pp. 5–6, Section 1.2.1, linear and nonlinear discussion].",
      "Discontinuities are expected in this setting, and classical differentiability at a jump is not a condition of the initial-data definition [printed pp. 4–5, Section 1.1.2; printed p. 5, equation (1.11)].",
